rcSet_subset_chordSet","d":""}]},{"p":"APAP/Prereqs/Bohr/Basic.lean","t":"Basic","s":"","i":["APAP/Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Ring/Basic.lean"],"l":351,"n":[35,7,15],"h":[{"k":"def","n":"BohrSet","d":"A *Bohr set* `B` on an additive group `G` is a finite set of characters of `G`, called the *frequencies*, along with an extended non-negative real number for each frequency `ψ`, called the *width of `B` at `ψ`*."},{"k":"def","n":"ofEwidth","d":"Construct a Bohr set on a finite group given an extended width function."},{"k":"def","n":"ofWidth","d":"Construct a Bohr set on a finite group given a width function and a frequency set."},{"k":"def","n":"chordSet","d":"The set corresponding to a Bohr set `B` is `{x | ∀ ψ ∈ B.frequencies, ‖1 - ψ x‖ ≤ B.width ψ}`. This is the *chord-length* convention."},{"k":"def","n":"Elem","d":"Given the Bohr set `B`, `B.Elem` is the `Type` of elements of `B`."},{"k":"def","n":"rank","d":"The rank of a Bohr set is the number of characters which have finite width."}]},{"p":"APAP/Prereqs/Bohr/Regular.lean","t":"Regular","s":"","i":["APAP/Prereqs/Bohr/Basic.lean"],"l":25,"n":[1,1,0],"h":[{"k":"theorem","n":"regularity","d":"**Bohr Set Regularity**. Any Bohr set can be dilated by a small amount to become a regular Bohr set."},{"k":"def","n":"IsRegular","d":"A Bohr set `B` is *regular* if the dilates of `B` by numbers close to `1` are of comparable size to `B`."}]},{"p":"APAP/Prereqs/Chang.lean","t":"Chang's lemma","s":"","i":["APAP/Prereqs/Energy.lean","APAP/Prereqs/LargeSpec.lean","APAP/Prereqs/Rudin.lean"],"l":208,"n":[9,1,0],"h":[{"k":"theorem","n":"chang","d":"**Chang's lemma**."}]},{"p":"APAP/Prereqs/Convolution/Compact.lean","t":"Convolution in the compact normalisation","s":"This file defines several versions of the discrete convolution of functions with the compact normalisation.","i":["APAP/Prereqs/Convolution/Discrete/Defs.lean"],"l":254,"n":[34,2,0],"h":[{"k":"def","n":"trivNChar","d":"The trivial character."},{"k":"def","n":"iterCConv","